    "productType": "ACTIVITY",
    "name": "Wild Escapes Tasmania｜Night Safari & Southern Light",
    "shortDescription": "南極光｜夜晚星空｜野生動物｜野性呼喚｜塔斯深夜活動\r\nSouthern Light, Starry starry night, Wild Night & Wildlife.\r\n",
    "description": "<h3><br></h3><h3><p><strong>\"Under the moonlight of Tasmania, illuminate the story of your journey.\"</strong><br><br><strong>\"Step into the night of Hobart and capture the moment you’ll never want to forget.\"</strong><br><br><strong>\"Southern stars, nocturnal wildlife, and lantern-lit heritage streets — your exclusive night tour experience in Tasmania, Australia.\"</strong></p><p><br></p></h3><h3><b><u>Tasmania<br>Aurora Viewing Guide x Wild Night Animal Exploration</u></b></h3><h3><p><u>Night Sky Tasmania:</u></p><p>Tasmania<br>is one of the best locations in Australia to witness the Southern Lights<br>(Aurora Australia).</p><p>&nbsp;Here is a comprehensive guide to the best viewing spots,<br>optimal viewing times, and essential tips.</p><p><u>Animal Exploration:</u></p><p>Night creatures come out during the night time!!!</p><p>Especially for the wild wallabies, and the possums. You have a greater chance to spot them during the starry starry night.</p><p>Some other animals like Platypus, Ring-tailed possums, Twany frogmouth, Masked Owl...etc.&nbsp;</p><p>You may also have a chance to spot one of those cute Tasmanian night people.</p></h3><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>Recommended Viewing Spots:</h3><h3><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>South Bruny Island:</strong></p><p>Cape Bruny Lighthouse offers an excellent vantage point with<br>minimal light pollution and expansive views.</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Hobart:</strong></p><p>Kunanyi / Mount Wellington summit area provides a sweeping view of<br>the southern coastline.</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Cockle Creek:</strong></p><p>The southernmost village in Tasmania, offering open, dark skies,<br>making it a prime spot for aurora viewing.</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Seven Mile Beach:</strong></p><p>Close to Hobart, a convenient spot for a quick aurora viewing<br>session.</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>South Arm Peninsula:</strong></p><p>Minimal light pollution and a beautiful southern coastline view.</p></h3><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>Best Viewing Times:</h3><h3><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>The aurora is most active in autumn and winter (May to August).</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>New moon periods provide the darkest skies for optimal viewing.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Aurora activity peaks when the Kp index reaches 4-5 or higher.</p></h3><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>How to Track Aurora Activity:</h3><h3><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><strong>Aurora Forecast App:</strong>&nbsp;Monitor Kp<br>index and cloud cover.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><strong>Space Weather Live:</strong>&nbsp;Check<br>real-time solar wind data and aurora forecasts.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><strong>Facebook Groups:</strong>&nbsp;Join<br>Tasmania aurora tracking communities for real-time updates.</p></h3><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>Aurora Photography Tips:</h3><h3><p>Camera<br>Settings:</p><p>&nbsp;Aperture:<br>f/2.8 or wider</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;ISO:<br>1600-3200</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Exposure<br>Time: 10-20 seconds</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Use a tripod<br>to prevent camera shake</p><p>Recommended<br>Gear:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Warm<br>clothing, hot drinks</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Headlamp<br>(with a red light option)</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Camping chair<br>or blanket</p></h3><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>Safety Tips:</h3><h3><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Inform friends or family about your itinerary before heading to<br>remote areas.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Ensure your phone is fully charged and bring extra batteries.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Be cautious around cliffs and shorelines, especially during high<br>tides.</p><p><br></p></h3><h3>✨&nbsp;<strong><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">觀星 × 南極光 × 夜間野生動物探索</span></strong></h3><h3><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"><br></span></h3><h3><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">在塔斯馬尼亞南部，當夜幕降臨，真正的奇幻旅程才剛剛開始。<br></span><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">這裡遠離光害，天空清澈透明，是南半球最適合觀星與觀賞南極光的祕境之一。</span></h3><h3><br></h3><h3>「在塔斯馬尼亞的月光下，點亮你旅程的故事。」<br><br>「走進霍巴特的夜，拍下你最不想忘記的那一刻。」<br><br>「南半球星空、野生動物、提燈古街——為你打造澳洲限定的塔州夜遊體驗。」</h3><br><h3><u>塔斯馬尼亞極光觀賞指南</u></h3><p>塔斯馬尼亞是澳洲最佳觀賞極光（Aurora Australis）的地點之一，</p><p>以下為您提供最佳觀賞點、觀賞時機及觀賞技巧。</p><h3><br></h3><h3>觀賞地點推薦：</h3><br><ol><li><p><strong>南布魯尼島 (South Bruny Island)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Cape Bruny Lighthouse 是觀賞極光的絕佳地點，沒有光害，視野遼闊。</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>霍巴特 (Hobart)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Kunanyi / Mount Wellington 山頂區域，可以俯瞰整個南部海岸線。</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Cockle Creek</strong></p><ul><li><p>塔斯馬尼亞最南端的村莊，開闊無光害，是捕捉極光的最佳地點之一。</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Seven Mile Beach</strong></p><ul><li><p>離霍巴特不遠，適合快速前往觀賞。</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>South Arm Peninsula</strong></p><ul><li><p>沒有光害且風景優美，可以看見完整的南方海岸線。</p></li></ul></li></ol><h3><br></h3><h3>極光觀賞時間：</h3><ul><li><p>極光多發生於秋冬季節（5月至8月）。</p></li><li><p>新月期間光害最少，適合觀賞極光。</p></li><li><p>極光活動高峰期：磁暴指數（Kp指數）達到 4-5 或以上時，觀賞機會較高。</p></li></ul><h3><br></h3><h3>如何獲取即時極光資訊：</h3><p><strong>Aurora Forecast App：</strong> 追蹤Kp指數與雲量覆蓋。</p><p><strong>Space Weather Live：</strong> 查看即時太陽風數據與極光預測。</p><p><strong>Facebook群組：</strong> 塔斯馬尼亞極光觀賞社群會即時分享觀測訊息。&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>拍攝極光建議 :</p><p>相機設置：</p><ul><li><p>光圈：f/2.8或更大</p></li><li><p>ISO：1600-3200</p></li><li><p>曝光時間：10-20秒</p></li><li><p>使用三腳架避免晃動</p></li></ul><p>建議攜帶：</p><ul><li><p>保暖衣物、熱飲</p></li><li><p>頭燈（具紅光功能）</p></li><li><p>露營椅或毯子</p></li></ul><h3><br></h3><h3>安全建議：</h3><ul><li><p>前往偏僻地區前，務必告知親友行程。</p></li><li><p>確保手機充飽電並帶備備用電池。</p></li><li><p>注意潮汐情況，避免靠近海岸懸崖。</p></li></ul><br><ul><br></ul><p><br><br><br></p><p><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br></p><p></p>",
